        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Your Foundation in Action</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/47465.webp" alt="Your Foundation in Action" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>With supporters like you, we’ve elevated lives in Teton Valley over the last year through <span><strong>Youth Philanthropy</strong></span>, <span><strong>Competitive Grant Programs</strong></span>, and <span><strong>Nonprofit Workshops</strong></span>.</p>
<p><img data-opt-id=1496989880   decoding="async" title="newsletter 1" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20100%%20100%%22%20width%3D%22100%%22%20height%3D%22100%%22%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%22100%%22%20height%3D%22100%%22%20fill%3D%22%23f8f5ec%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E?__nocache__=1" alt="newsletter 1" width="600" height="150" align="none" border="0" hspace="5" vspace="10" /><noscript><img data-opt-id=1496989880  decoding="async" title="newsletter 1" src="https://img-ak.verticalresponse.com/media/8/e/7/8e7cc30df0/9ad6226769/newsletter%20cftv-events/ed-exchange/1.jpg?__nocache__=1" alt="newsletter 1" width="600" height="150" align="none" border="0" hspace="5" vspace="10" /></noscript><br />
<span><strong>Youth Philanthropy</strong></span> brings the Community Foundation into the classroom of high school seniors with three classes that serve to illustrate philanthropy in action and bring awareness to the local nonprofit landscape. In our most recent cycle, these emerging community leaders worked through real-world budget constraints and critical community needs to <span><strong>award $5K</strong></span> to <span><strong>6 nonprofits</strong></span>. Students gain a palpable sense of responsibility for their community and the importance of charitable giving through this program.</p>
<p><img data-opt-id=1329869769   decoding="async" title="newsletter 2" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20100%%20100%%22%20width%3D%22100%%22%20height%3D%22100%%22%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%22100%%22%20height%3D%22100%%22%20fill%3D%22%23f8f5ec%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E?__nocache__=1" alt="newsletter 2" width="600" height="150" align="none" border="0" hspace="5" vspace="10" /><noscript><img data-opt-id=1329869769  decoding="async" title="newsletter 2" src="https://img-ak.verticalresponse.com/media/8/e/7/8e7cc30df0/9ad6226769/newsletter%20cftv-events/ed-exchange/2.jpg?__nocache__=1" alt="newsletter 2" width="600" height="150" align="none" border="0" hspace="5" vspace="10" /></noscript><br />
Our <span><strong>2018</strong> <strong>Competitive Grants Program</strong></span> funded <span><strong>13 nonprofit grant projects</strong></span> with a total of <span><strong>$47,805</strong></span>. These funds promptly went to work to improve meals at Seniors West of the Tetons, address a lack of affordable childcare during summer months, stabilize local aquifer levels, and provide accessible ramps at the Teton Valley Museum – to name a few. The scope and breadth of work covered by these funds were both impressive and immediate.</p>
<p><img data-opt-id=477514375   decoding="async" title="newsletter 3" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20100%%20100%%22%20width%3D%22100%%22%20height%3D%22100%%22%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%22100%%22%20height%3D%22100%%22%20fill%3D%22%23f8f5ec%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E?__nocache__=1" alt="newsletter 3" width="600" height="150" align="none" border="0" hspace="5" vspace="10" /><noscript><img data-opt-id=477514375  decoding="async" title="newsletter 3" src="https://img-ak.verticalresponse.com/media/8/e/7/8e7cc30df0/9ad6226769/newsletter%20tin-cup/2024-tin-cup-event/3.jpg?__nocache__=1" alt="newsletter 3" width="600" height="150" align="none" border="0" hspace="5" vspace="10" /></noscript><br />
The <span><strong>Tin Cup Challenge</strong></span>, our cornerstone grant program, celebrated further success in its 11<sup>th</sup>year, raising over <span><strong>$1.5 million</strong></span> for <span><strong>46 local nonprofits</strong></span> and <span><strong>$12.7 million</strong></span> to date. This program uniquely trains our community to give annually, while simultaneously providing sustaining funds for many of our local organizations.  With the generosity of Challengers, the Foundation was able to award a <span><strong>Matching Grant of 50%</strong></span> for the first $25K that each organization raised this year.</p>
<p><img data-opt-id=1919303858   decoding="async" title="newsletter 4" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20100%%20100%%22%20width%3D%22100%%22%20height%3D%22100%%22%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%22100%%22%20height%3D%22100%%22%20fill%3D%22%23f8f5ec%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E?__nocache__=1" alt="newsletter 4" width="600" height="150" align="none" border="0" hspace="5" vspace="10" /><noscript><img data-opt-id=1919303858  decoding="async" title="newsletter 4" src="https://img-ak.verticalresponse.com/media/8/e/7/8e7cc30df0/9ad6226769/newsletter%20tin-cup/2024-tin-cup-event/4.jpg?__nocache__=1" alt="newsletter 4" width="600" height="150" align="none" border="0" hspace="5" vspace="10" /></noscript><br />
<span><strong>Nonprofit workshops</strong></span> hosted by the Community Foundation help advance best practices across the local nonprofit landscape. Both board and staff members benefit from these in-depth, focused sessions that provide attendees with best practices, tools, resources and ready plans that educate, inspire and push the crucial missions of our nonprofits forward.</p>
<p>Together, we&#8217;ve leveraged Teton Valley&#8217;s nonprofit landscape to reflect the majesty of the mountains that surround us.  With a year-end gift, you support the time and energy it takes to provide these programs to our community on an annual basis.</p>
<p>Peace and prosperity,</p>
<p>Tim Adams<br />
Executive Director</p>
